{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review animal welfare regulations to prevent cross-border puppy farming",
        "additional_details": "We call on the Government to amend the law to:\r\n\r\n1. Mandate a point-of-birth handover, legally requiring all puppy sales to happen at the exact physical property where the litter was born making long-distance retail shipping illegal.\r\n2. Prohibit local authorities from issuing separate, individual breeding licences to different corporate entities or individuals operating out of the same physical address/farm complex.\r\n",
        "background": "We call on the Government to take action to ensure that puppies are not being transported between different parts of the UK from irresponsible breeders, so called \u201cpuppy farms\u201d. We believe a change to the law is needed to ensure there are no \u201cloopholes\u201d in the law.",
